  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The regional project on Peace and Security in the Great Lakes Region &#xbf; Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Action is the second phase of a project coming to an end in 2022. Its Overall Objective is to contribute to the consolidation of peace, security and mineral resources governance in the Great Lakes Region (GLR). This will be achieved via two Specific Objectives (SOs) : 1) By strengthening&amp;nbsp;the contribution of the International Conference on the Great Lakes Region (ICGLR) to conflict prevention and resolution in the region; 2) By contributing to the improvement of the control of the mineral sectors in ICGLR Member States.The two areas of focus of the Action are domains in which ICGLR has a distinct added value: 1) It is the sole African-led forum mandated to bring together the states of Eastern, Central, and Southern Africa around the search for concerted solutions to the challenges of peace and security in the GLR; 2) It is the only regional platform that has a strong political mandate, a renewed backing from Member States and a degree of technical expertise to work on curbing conflict financing linked to the minerals sector, via its Regional Initiative against the Illegal Exploitation of Natural Resources (RINR).The Action will contribute to further mitigate the conflict triggers that prevent the Great Lakes Region from realising its full human and economic development potential.&amp;nbsp;OS1 will be achieved through two outputs: 1) the reinforcement of ICGLR&#xbf;s Enhanced Joint Observation Mission (EJVM), tasked to prevent border clashes, investigate incidents, and prepare the ground for the repatriation of foreign combatants; and 2) the development of an ICGLR early warning mechanism. OS2 will be achieved through three outputs: 1) the revision of the RINR and development of guidance for new instruments; 2) decisive action to implement ICGLR&#xbf;s gold strategy; and 3) technical work to digitise mining certificates and adapt them in live with the evolving international due diligence standards.</narrative>
  </description>
